WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.937
When zinc sits in copper sulfate solution, the electrons jump straight from the zinc to the copper ions, and the energy is lost as heat.

00:00:08.537 --> 00:00:19.173
A galvanic cell keeps the two apart. Now the electrons can only get from the zinc to the copper ions by travelling through a wire. That flow of electrons is an electric current.

00:00:21.673 --> 00:00:30.877
Here is a zinc electrode in zinc nitrate solution and a copper electrode in copper nitrate solution. Which electrode is the anode? Decide now.

00:00:35.477 --> 00:00:50.053
The zinc electrode. Zinc, at minus zero comma seven six volts, is a stronger reducing agent than copper, at plus zero comma three four volts. So zinc is oxidised, and the anode is where oxidation takes place.

00:00:50.653 --> 00:00:53.839
The half-cell with the lower electrode potential is always the anode.

00:00:56.339 --> 00:01:00.366
At the anode, zinc gives zinc two plus, plus two electrons.

00:01:00.966 --> 00:01:05.398
At the cathode, copper two plus, plus two electrons, gives copper.

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:16.921
Add them and the electrons cancel. Zinc plus copper two plus gives zinc two plus plus copper. Use a single arrow every time. A double arrow costs a mark.

00:01:19.421 --> 00:01:29.825
Electrons leave the zinc anode and flow through the wire to the copper cathode. They never enter the solutions or the salt bridge. In there, the charge is carried by ions.

00:01:30.425 --> 00:01:39.355
What would you see? The zinc electrode gets thinner. A reddish-brown layer of copper forms on the copper electrode, and the blue colour slowly fades.

00:01:39.955 --> 00:01:46.574
Name the electrode, not the half-cell. The examiners did not accept the half-cell or the solution as the anode.

00:01:49.074 --> 00:02:06.495
Cell notation writes the whole cell in one line. The anode goes on the left, the salt bridge is a double line in the middle, and the cathode goes on the right. Zinc, zinc two plus, double line, copper two plus, copper. No coefficients and no electrons.

00:02:08.995 --> 00:02:24.439
The emf of the cell is E theta cathode minus E theta anode. Zero comma three four, minus bracket minus zero comma seven six, gives one comma one zero volts. Positive, so the reaction is spontaneous under standard conditions.

00:02:25.039 --> 00:02:30.648
Write the formula, substitute with brackets round the negative value, and give the answer with its unit.

00:02:33.148 --> 00:02:41.138
Open the galvanic cell lab. Pick two half-cells, predict the anode and the direction of the electrons, then press play and check.
